---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { siteFromHost } from '../../content';

const site = siteFromHost();
const path = '/compare/klaviyo-vs-yotpo-email-sms';
const title = "Klaviyo vs Yotpo Email & SMS: migration and retained modules";
const desc = "A Shopify migration decision after Yotpo Email and SMS retirement: retain useful review and loyalty data while choosing a messaging owner.";

const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Can I trial Yotpo Email against Klaviyo now?",
    "answer": "Yotpo announced retirement of Email and SMS, and its product endpoint reports decommissioning. Evaluate a replacement sender rather than a new Yotpo Email trial."
  },
  {
    "question": "Must I replace Yotpo Reviews too?",
    "answer": "The messaging retirement does not establish that Reviews or Loyalty have ended. Decide separately whether retained modules and their data integrations meet your needs."
  },
  {
    "question": "What decides Klaviyo fit?",
    "answer": "The required events, review and loyalty fields, exclusions and operator workflow must work in your account. Supplier feature descriptions do not establish migration parity."
  }
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />

  <section class="py-14 md:py-20">
    <div class="container">
      <nav class="mb-8 text-sm">
        <a class="link" href="/compare">Comparisons</a>
        <span class="mx-2 text-[#5d3a1d]">/</span>
        <span class="text-[#5d3a1d]">Klaviyo vs Yotpo Email & SMS</span>
      </nav>

      <header class="max-w-4xl">
        <p class="editorial-kicker">Head-to-head</p>
        <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Klaviyo vs Yotpo Email & SMS: migration and retained modules</h1>
        <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9 text-[#4a2d17]">Yotpo Email & SMS is no longer a live alternative to trial against Klaviyo. For a store arriving from an old comparison, the useful decision is how to rebuild messaging while preserving the review and loyalty context it still needs.</p>
      </header>

      <article class="prose-shopify mt-14 max-w-4xl">
        <p><em>Source descriptions checked November 24, 2026. Proposed exercises below are not completed tests or merchant results.</em></p>
        <h2>What changed</h2>
        <p>Yotpo’s <a href="https://www.yotpo.com/blog/email-sms-migration-partners/">September 2025 migration announcement</a> scheduled full Email and SMS deprecation for December 31, 2025. Its <a href="https://email-and-sms.yotpo.com/">product endpoint</a> now reports decommissioning. That scope is the messaging products; it does not establish that Reviews or Loyalty have ended. Do not buy or plan a new Yotpo Email deployment from an old feature matrix.</p>
        <h2>Where Klaviyo fits</h2>
        <p>The <a href="https://apps.shopify.com/klaviyo-email-marketing">Klaviyo developer listing</a> advertises Shopify data, segmentation and automated messaging. These advertised capabilities make it a candidate for lifecycle ownership, not proof that an old Yotpo flow imports intact. Separate selecting a sender from deciding whether to retain a review collection or points program.</p>
        <h2>Map the review request boundary</h2>
        <p>Inventory order confirmation, delivery follow-up, review request, reminder and thank-you messages. Assign one owner to each. A delivery-based request must have a reliable delivery signal; an order-created timestamp is not an equivalent replacement. Record the behavior when shipment is split, a product is refunded or the customer has already reviewed it.</p>
        <h2>Proposed exercise: review status arrives late</h2>
        <p>This exercise has not been run here. Use an authorized test profile and a sample order. Let a review-status update arrive after entry into a proposed Klaviyo follow-up. Check whether the next message re-evaluates eligibility. Repeat with a missing product identifier. A safe fallback is to omit an unverified review block rather than attach praise to the wrong variant.</p>
        <h2>Loyalty data is a separate contract</h2>
        <p>List the exact fields an email needs: balance, tier, expiry date, redemption link and last update. Establish which retained loyalty system owns them and what the integration actually supplies. A tier label alone cannot calculate spend to the next tier. Avoid copying balances into a second writable ledger; stale incentives can create customer support disputes.</p>
        <h2>Rebuild cart and winback deliberately</h2>
        <p>Recreate cart eligibility, purchase exclusions, coupon restrictions and frequency rules before importing decorative review content. Distinguish cart and checkout events. Keep an inventory of welcome, postpurchase and winback messages so retiring a sender does not leave a forgotten scheduled campaign or duplicate review reminder active elsewhere.</p>
        <h2>Compare costs without a fictional suite discount</h2>
        <p>Obtain a Klaviyo quote for the actual reachable audience and planned channels. Keep retained review and loyalty charges on both sides of the comparison; include integration support, template work and data recovery. A sunk module subscription does not make a retired email service available, and attributed revenue is not evidence of incremental profit.</p>
        <h2>Cutover acceptance</h2>
        <p>Preserve accessible exports, suppression history and permission evidence before disconnecting anything. Confirm available export or recovery options with the supplier rather than assuming a retired dashboard still works. Release a replacement flow only after checking sender identity, links, exclusions and message ownership. Keep a rollback plan that does not depend on reactivating a retired service.</p>
      </article>

      <div class="mt-10 max-w-4xl text-sm">
        <p class="font-black text-[#24170f]">Related comparisons</p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          <a class="link" href="/compare/omnisend-vs-yotpo-email-sms">Omnisend vs Yotpo</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/marsello-vs-yotpo-email-sms">Marsello vs Yotpo</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/klaviyo-vs-omnisend">Klaviyo vs Omnisend</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/for/beauty">Email apps for beauty stores</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/use-cases/abandoned-cart">Abandoned cart playbook</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Klaviyo vs Yotpo Email & SMS FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
